From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:07:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] husky: values stock sets that our build left at the
 AOSP default

A stock-vs-build comparison of every static overlay's values (stock
CP3A.261005.005 against the target packages' effective values in our
build) found these left at the AOSP default, or overridden. Each overlay
copies stock's values from its APKs (rro2xml.py):
- framework (priority 2): pin the camera app, compile Play Store in
  pre-reboot dexopt's synchronous phase, Play Protect's dynamic
  instrumentation consumer (OdadPrebuilt), and stock's 3440x1600 external
  display peak (vendor/pixel-style's Pixelframework-res sets 3840x2160 at
  priority 1, tied with zuma's stock value)
- SystemUI: the screenshot Edit button opens Markup, the Files button opens
  Files by Google, Quick Share copy, the avatar picker we ship
  (com.google.android.avatarpicker, not com.android.avatarpicker), and Google
  Home first in device controls
- Settings: Google search and TalkBack slices, network list aggregation
- Wi-Fi: stock's 5 GHz scoring thresholds (bad -80, entry -77; AOSP -90/-85
  kept a weak 5 GHz network much longer)
- Photo picker: Google Photos as the cloud media provider
Same as cheetah's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
